# MiBench is built and run on the Linux VM. Normalize all text to LF in the
# repo and on checkout everywhere, so scripts, Makefiles, source, and text
# inputs work on the VM regardless of each machine's core.autocrlf setting.
# git auto-detects binary files (by NUL bytes) and leaves those untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Audio/image inputs that must stay byte-exact. Marked binary explicitly as a
# safeguard, so line-ending conversion can never corrupt them even if a file
# happens to contain no NUL bytes in the region git samples.
*.pcm   binary
*.adpcm binary
*.gsm   binary
*.au    binary
*.wav   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.bmp   binary
*.mp3   binary
